# The generated newsletter archive is checksummed byte-for-byte: every file's
# sha256 is recorded in `lib/data/newsletter-archive/index.json` and re-checked
# by `scripts/mailchimp/archive-guard.test.ts`, which is how a hand-edit to a
# GENERATED file becomes visible. Git must therefore not rewrite the bytes.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` — the default on Windows — turns every LF
# into CRLF on checkout, so the guard goes red on a fresh clone here while CI,
# on Linux, stays green. A checksum that depends on which machine cloned the
# repository is not a checksum.
lib/data/newsletter-archive/*.html -text
lib/data/newsletter-archive/index.json -text
